To fix the compilation errors, we need to add the necessary using directives and assembly references. We also need to make sure that the `AofTaskStore` and `ClusterProvider` classes are accessible from the test project.

Here's an updated version of the test file:

```csharp
using Xunit;
using Moq;
using Microsoft.Extensions.Logging;
using Garnet.cluster; // Add the necessary namespace

public class AofTaskStoreTests
{
    [Fact]
    public void TryAddReplicationTask_LogsError_WhenStartAddressIsLessThanTruncatedUntil()
    {
        // Arrange
        var loggerMock = new Mock<ILogger>();
        var clusterProvider = new ClusterProvider(); // Create a new instance of ClusterProvider
        var aofTaskStore = new AofTaskStore(clusterProvider, logger: loggerMock.Object);
        aofTaskStore.TruncatedUntil = 10;
        var startAddress = 5;

        // Act
        aofTaskStore.TryAddReplicationTask("remoteNodeId", startAddress, out _);

        // Assert
        loggerMock.Verify(l => l.LogError(It.IsAny<Exception>(), It.IsAny<string>(), It.IsAny<object[]>()), Times.Once);
    }

    [Fact]
    public void TryAddReplicationTask_LogsError_WhenExceptionIsThrown()
    {
        // Arrange
        var loggerMock = new Mock<ILogger>();
        var clusterProvider = new ClusterProvider(); // Create a new instance of ClusterProvider
        var aofTaskStore = new AofTaskStore(clusterProvider, logger: loggerMock.Object);
        var startAddress = 10;

        // Act
        aofTaskStore.TryAddReplicationTask("remoteNodeId", startAddress, out _);

        // Assert
        loggerMock.Verify(l => l.LogError(It.IsAny<Exception>(), It.IsAny<string>(), It.IsAny<object[]>()), Times.Once);
    }
}
```

If the `AofTaskStore` and `ClusterProvider` classes are in a different assembly, you may need to add a reference to that assembly in your test project.

Also, make sure that the `AofTaskStore` class is public and has a public constructor that takes a `ClusterProvider` instance and an `ILogger` instance.

If you're still having issues, you may need to use the `apply_refactor` tool to make the `AofTaskStore` class more testable. For example, you could use the `make_virtual` transform to make the `TryAddReplicationTask` method virtual, which would allow you to override it in a test subclass.

